6.2.4    Claiming rewards for all delegators may exceed limits
     File(s): src/validator_registry/validator_registry.cairo
     Description: The _claim_rewards_for_all_delegators(...) function may exceed the storage write limit. Starknet has a 2000 storage
     write limit per transaction. Claiming rewards for all delegators has a loop through all delegators and calls the claim_rewards(...) function
     on the delegators’ contract. Suppose there are more than 100 delegators registered for the validator. This function may revert and block
     the reward claiming.

 1   fn _claim_rewards_for_all_delegators(
 2       ref self: ContractState, validator: ContractAddress, token: ContractAddress,
 3   ) -> u128 {
 4       let delegator_count = self.get_total_delegators_for_validator(validator, token);
 5       let mut i: u32 = 0;
 6       let mut total_claim_amount = 0_u128;
 7       // @audit-issue: Loop through all delegators
 8       while i != delegator_count {
 9           let delegator = self.delegator_mapping.read((validator, token, i));
10           assert(delegator.is_non_zero(), Errors::DELEGATOR_NOT_FOUND);
11           let disp = IDelegatorDispatcher { contract_address: delegator };
12           total_claim_amount += disp.claim_rewards(token);
13           i += 1;
14       }
15
16       total_claim_amount
17   }

     Recommendation(s): Consider adding initialized check for those functions.
     Status: Fixed
     Update from the client: Fixed in 633dedc

