6.3.4    Claiming rewards for validators can miss epoches
     File(s): src/validator_registry/validator_registry.cairo
     Description: Everyone can claim rewards for validators with the function claim_rewards_for_validator(...). However, the claim
     was triggered by the _should_claim_validator(...) function. This function gets the current epoch from the staking contract and
     then checks the validators’ last epoch. If last_epoch != previous_epoch, then it returns true, and the caller function calls _claim_-
     rewards_for_all_delegators(...) to claim rewards.

 1   fn _should_claim_validator(
 2       self: @ContractState, validator: ContractAddress, token: ContractAddress,
 3   ) -> (bool, u64) {
 4       let staking_contract = self.staking_contract.read();
 5       let curr_epoch = staking_contract.get_current_epoch();
 6

 7       let previous_epoch = if (curr_epoch > 0) {
 8           curr_epoch - 1
 9       } else {
10           0
11       };
12

13       let val_info = self.validator_token_info.read((validator, token));
14       let last_epoch = val_info.last_epoch;
15       // @audit-issue It can miss epoches
16       if last_epoch == previous_epoch {
17           return (false, previous_epoch);
18       }
19       return (true, previous_epoch);
20   }

     But if the validator has not claimed rewards for some epochs, these can not be claimed. For example, if current_epoch = 5 and the
     validator last_epoch = 2, the function will claim only for the fourth epoch and then update the validator’s last_epoch to 4. So, third
     epoch rewards can not be claimed anymore.
     Recommendation(s): Consider changing reward claim mechanism.
     Status: Unresolved

     Update from the client: Validator reward claims cannot miss epochs because when anyone calls the claim reward function on the pool
     contract, it automatically claims all accumulated rewards up to the current epoch. The reward claiming logic remains identical to the
     current production implementation—it has simply been relocated and modified to support multiple validators rather than single validator
     operations.

